polygram — installation

polygram is standard-library Python (3.8+) with a POSIX shell entry point.
There is nothing to compile and no third-party dependencies.

Get it
------
The public source is https://code.bru.st/corwin/vibrobeast (git clone, or a
release archive from the same page).

First run, in this order
------------------------
    sh bin/polygram doctor         # check the runtime and the workspace
    UNSIGNED=1 make dist           # mint dist/: .skill bundles + the plugin
                                   # (UNSIGNED=1: no signing key needed)
    make check                     # the python test suite

Every script is run through `sh` on purpose: a clone made by git on Windows
leaves no execute bit, and `sh bin/polygram` works either way.
`bin/polygram` locates the package from its own path and runs
`python3 -m polygram`. Override the interpreter with PYTHON=python3.12.

`doctor` notes, and does not fail on, an extern that is registered in
externs.json but not fetched here (externs/ is not part of a clone); run
`sh bin/polygram extern sync` to fetch the git ones.

Without the author's C4 tree (C4_ROOT), `make dist` says what it leaves out:
the canon skills, the secrets scan, and the publication read are each named
as skipped; `make garden` says it needs C4 and exits 0.

Verify
------
Signed skills are signed with Corwin Brust's OpenPGP key, fingerprint

    ECE7 7CF4 17C7 6C1A CFCE  7C2B 5B61 3551 1580 F007

The key is in this tree as skills/ECE77CF417C76C1ACFCE7C2B5B6135511580F007.asc
and on keys.openpgp.org. Import it and check the fingerprint gpg prints:

    gpg --import skills/ECE77CF417C76C1ACFCE7C2B5B6135511580F007.asc
    gpg --fingerprint ECE77CF417C76C1ACFCE7C2B5B6135511580F007

then verify a skill (tiered: "signature valid", UNVERIFIED-AUTHOR for a
hash-only manifest, or TREE CHANGED / SIGNATURE FAILED):

    sh skills/skill-sign/scripts/skill-sign.sh verify skills/NAME

and, after a mint, the plugin's bytes against its MANIFEST:

    sh dist/vibrobeast/check.sh

Put it on PATH (optional)
-------------------------
    export PATH="$PWD/bin:$PATH"

Tests
-----
    make check                                  # = python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
    for t in tests/*-tests.sh; do sh "$t"; done # the shell suites
    sh bin/gd1ck --no-c4                        # everything, one verdict per item

A suite that cannot run here (no dist/ yet, no C4 tree, no ruby >= 3) prints
SKIP and exits 77; bin/gd1ck reports it as SKIPPED -- not a pass, not a failure.

The Info manual
---------------
    make info                      # builds doc/polygram.info (needs makeinfo)
    info -f doc/polygram.info

Requirements
------------
    POSIX /bin/sh, Python 3.8+     everything
    make                           make dist / check / garden / kit
    sha256sum                      skill-sign.sh manifest/verify and check.sh
                                   (both also take shasum -a 256);
                                   tests/*-tests.sh (sha256sum itself)
    zip, unzip                     skill-sign.sh bundle / unbundle
    gpg                            signing (make dist without UNSIGNED=1) and
                                   the signature tier of skill-sign.sh verify
    perl                           tests/mcp-tests.sh, the Perl chain reader
                                   (servers/bin/dl2-verify.pl), tests/*.pl
    ruby >= 3                      tests only: tests/boundary-secrets-tests.sh
                                   (SKIPs without it)
    git                            polygram extern sync; bin/release
    makeinfo (GNU Texinfo)         make info
